    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive base-running and high-floor match-ups. **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite 85.94 rating; facing Lorenzen, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 14% park factor boost and prime batting order positioning, making him our primary engine for the day. **James Wood** follows closely at 76.28, capitalizing on a weak 4.77 xERA matchup and a 10% boost for hitting out of the leadoff spot. We are also leaning heavily into **Mickey Moniak** (73.50) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71), both of whom benefit from significant park-induced inflation and favorable dynamic platoon splits. **Brice Turang** remains a critical start at 70.33, not just for his batting order placement, but because the opposing pitcher's slow delivery speed significantly increases his probability for a high-value stolen base attempt.\n\nThe decision to keep **Kyle Karros** on the bench was the most difficult of the morning. While **Kyle Karros** carries a respectable 44.88 score and enjoys the same park-driven upside as **Mickey Moniak**, his lower batting order position and the negative impact of facing Soroka\u2019s specific profile pushed him just below our threshold for active roster consideration. Elsewhere, we remain cautious of the volatility in the lineup; while **Dalton Rushing** and **Gabriel Moreno** are locked in as our catchers, their reliance on favorable platoon dynamics against Rodriguez and Lorenzen respectively means their floor is slightly lower than a standard corner infielder like **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who is slated for a strong outing against Pallante with the benefit of favorable winds. We continue to monitor the status of **Jose Caballero** and **Trevor Story**, who remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on our active depth to keep the pressure on our divisional opponents. With **Zach McKinstry** also relegated to the bench due to a difficult matchup against Gausman, our focus remains on maximizing plate appearances from the top-to-middle order hitters to ensure we remain competitive across all five categories.",
